# Repo-declared flags for scripts/check-public-repo-secrets.py, appended by the
# canonical .github/workflows/{commit-message-scan,issue-body-scan}.yml. One
# flag per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# This file exists because those two workflows are VENDORED MIRRORS of
# dotfiles/github/workflows/, byte-identical across 17 repos. Hand-editing a
# mirror to add these flags worked and went green, and the next
# `propagate-mirrors.py --apply` would have silently stripped them and turned
# main red with nobody touching the repo. The flags live here instead, in a file
# the canonical reads and propagation never overwrites.

# hoiboy-uk IS public. Assert it: if .public-repo is ever deleted or renamed the
# scan would otherwise no-op and exit 0, retiring the leak gate while CI stayed
# green. Declared here rather than derived from `[ -f .public-repo ]`, because
# deriving it would drop the assertion in exactly the case it exists to catch.
--require-public

# This PUBLIC repo cannot hold the .secret-blocklist hashes manifest — the
# manifest maps opaque tokens to the literals they cover, so publishing it
# defeats the point. Without this flag the scanner exits 2 rather than report a
# clean it cannot back. The flag records the choice: the opaque tokens in
# .secret-blocklist stay unexpanded, so the business identifiers, dev-machine
# paths and internal repo names they cover are matched only if a document quotes
# the token verbatim. Credential and PII detection are shape-based and are NOT
# affected. Full coverage still runs locally in pre-commit and pre-publish,
# where the sibling dotfiles clone resolves the manifest.
--allow-degraded-blocklist
